---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for manufacturers | Decisive';
const description =
  'Which product actually makes money? We price the answer in dollars, in 14 days, on guarantee. Margin recovered 15% to 22% in 90 days at a $15M manufacturer.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Anchoring',
    body: 'Pricing anchored to input costs that moved years ago is the most common trapped margin on a factory floor, and the fastest to recover once the standard costs get re-run against reality.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Mental Accounting',
    body: 'A clean aggregate P&L hides which SKUs and lines carry the business and which quietly bleed. The product-line math never gets run, so the cross-subsidy compounds.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Loss Aversion',
    body: 'The largest customer is often the least profitable. The account you are most afraid to reprice is usually the one capping your margin, and the math never gets run because the answer feels dangerous.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For manufacturers and consumer products companies</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">Revenue is easy to see.</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">Which product makes money is not.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        The aggregate P&amp;L hides which products carry the business and which quietly bleed. <span class="dollar">We price the answer in dollars.</span> Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing where to look first.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Where the margin hides in a product business</span>
        <h2>The margin is on the floor. The P&amp;L can't see it.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Input-cost drift, phantom discounts, standard versus actual cost, product-line and SKU profitability, customer concentration: the numbers that decide which products deserve your capacity. Most product companies run for years without any of them allocated to reality.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Your books tell you what happened. They can't tell you what to do next.
        </div>
        <p>
          The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from. Everyone who touches your books is paid to serve something else: the filing, the close, the report. Nobody is paid to make the next call defensible, and that is the job we do.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps that hide inside a clean P&amp;L.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers through the decisions that produced them. Three of the six do the most damage in a product business. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one in dollars, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>Two product companies. The gap was never the market. It was the numbers.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Consumer products manufacturer, $25M revenue</span>
        <h4>The gap was never the market. It was the numbers.</h4>
        <p>
          Bankers' estimate was $25M to $35M, on books the owner didn't trust. Mispriced inputs, phantom discounts, and revenue never brought over. Pricing was anchored to costs that had moved years earlier, and the aggregate P&amp;L hid which products carried the business. We rebuilt the numbers and modeled the path forward.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Banker's estimate</span><span class="v">$25M to $35M</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Modeled path</span><span class="v accent">roughly $52M</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <span class="label">Manufacturer, $15M revenue</span>
        <h4>The account nobody would touch was the margin everyone was looking for.</h4>
        <p>
          The largest customer was the least profitable. The account felt untouchable, so the math never got run, and full cost allocation showed it was funded by everyone else. We repriced and reset terms instead of protecting the logo.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Least profitable account</span><span class="v">The largest one</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margins moved</span><span class="v accent">15% to 22%</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Time to recover</span><span class="v">90 days</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Decision Diagnostic and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Diagnostic promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you know what your money is actually doing, in dollars: the traps that are running, the recoverable value, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
